   326	## 4. Polynomial systems over \(\mathbf Q\)
   327	
   328	This section distinguishes an exact *node-local projection*, which is
   329	computable from the supplied data, from the unavailable source-exact jet
   330	fiber product.
   331	
   332	### 4.1 One non-bottom node
   333	
   334	Fix \((P,Q,A,b,\{u_i\}_{i=1}^r)\). Introduce quotient-root variables
   335	\(a_1,\ldots,a_r\), a monic q-only factor
   336	
   337	\[
   338	 H(z)=z^s+h_{s-1}z^{s-1}+\cdots+h_0,
   339	\]
   340	
   341	and nonzero leaders \(\lambda_p,\lambda_q\). Put
   342	
   343	\[
   344	 F(z)=\prod_{i=1}^r(z-a_i)^{u_i},\quad
   345	 R(z)=\prod_{i=1}^r(z-a_i),
   346	\]
   347	\[
   348	 p(\pi)=\lambda_p\pi^bF(\pi^A),\qquad
   349	 q(\pi)=\lambda_q\pi^eR(\pi^A)H(\pi^A).                       \tag{4.1}
   350	\]
   351	
   352	Squarefreeness forces \(e\in\{0,1\}\), fixed by \(Q\equiv e\pmod A\).
   353	The degree constraints are
   354	
   355	\[
   356	 P=b+A\sum_i u_i,\qquad Q=e+A(r+s).                            \tag{4.2}
   357	\]
   358	
   359	The ideal \(I_{P,Q,A,\mathbf u}\) is generated over \(\mathbf Q\) by every
   360	coefficient of
   361	
   362	\[
   363	 Pp q'-Qq p'-cp.                                               \tag{4.3}
   364	\]
   365	
   366	Equivalently, it is generated from the quotient expression (2.4). A convenient
   367	open-locus product is
   368	
   369	\[
   370	 U=\lambda_p\lambda_qc\,
   371	       R(0)H(0)\Disc(R)\Disc(H)\Res(R,H),                       \tag{4.4}
   372	\]
   373	
   374	with factors omitted when their polynomial has degree zero or when the zero
   375	orbit is intentionally present. Compute \((I:U^\infty)\), equivalently add
   376	\(TU-1\). The “\(p\) not a power of \(q\)” case is a discrete
   377	passport exclusion: since \(q\) is squarefree, the forbidden case is exactly
   378	equal supports with all multiplicities of \(p\) equal. It also follows from
   379	(4.3) once \(c\ne0\).
   380	
   381	This rational polynomial system avoids roots of unity by representing each
   382	nonzero orbit by \(z-a_i\). Actual sibling roots require
   383	\(r_i^A-a_i=0\), a primitive \(A\)-th root \(\zeta\), and the linear equations
   384	expressing the chosen chart representation under \(r_i\mapsto\zeta r_i\).
   385	The representation weights of the *child chart coefficients* are not printed
   386	on page 201. This is OPEN[GALOIS-CHART-MAP], folded into
   387	OPEN[SOURCE-JET-GLUING]; its bounded test is the same 16/12 first-band
   388	experiment in §7.4, including an explicit action matrix.
