   118	## 2. Task (1) — emit: descent, Φ, (8)–(13), SHAPE, system
   119	
   120	### 2.1 Descent (Prop 6.3 / 6.4)
   121	
   122	One step, `u_s = d_s − V_s = 1` required (else `US-GT-1`). Transformation,
   123	`SOURCE-READ` p.207 / charged `descent.py`:
   124	
   125	```text
   126	n' = n/d_s,  m' = m/d_s,  M_i' = M_i/d_s (i < s),  d_i' = d_i/d_s,
   127	V_i' = V_i (i < s),  k = v_s − u_s − 1,  s' = s − 1.
   128	```
   129	
   130	p.207 gate (this lane, identical to charged `descent_table.py`):
   131	
   132	```text
   133	  (64,48)                 -> (16,12) M2'=13 V2'=3 k=1  s'=2
   134	  (84,56) M2=64,V2=2      -> (21,14) M2'=16 V2'=2 k=1  s'=2
   135	  (84,56) M2=72,V2=5      -> (21,14) M2'=18 V2'=5 k=1  s'=2
   136	  (75,50) V2=3            -> (15,10) M2'=11 V2'=3 k=2  s'=2
   137	  (75,50) V2=2            -> (15,10) M2'=11 V2'=2 k=2  s'=2
   138	  (99,66)                 u_s=3  Prop 6.3 N/A
   139	```
   140	
   141	All five `u_s = 1` rows: `True`. G2/G3: `(15,10; k=4, M2'=4, V2'=1)` and
   142	`(21,14; k=2, M2'=8, V2'=1)`. G1: `u_s = 2`.
   143	
   144	### 2.2 Radii by Φ
   145	
   146	Charged closed rule, reproduced:
   147	
   148	> **Φ.** `δ_i' = (k+1) · Def 5.1(3)(n', m', M_2', V_2'; s' = 2)`.
   149	
   150	10/10 printed p.207 rationals MATCH (`shape.phi_s2`, same arithmetic as
   151	charged `phi_delta.py`). G2/G3: `(-1/2, 5/4)` and `(-1/4, 9/8)`.
   152	
   153	Convention: `t = x^{-1}`; `δ = min ord_t(τ_i − τ_j)` (Prop 5.1). Φ is
   154	Def 5.1(3) on the descended characteristic data, converted from the
   155	Jacobian-normalized parameter to that `t` by the factor `k+1`. Not a
   156	reindexing, not `δ_i' = δ_{i+1}`, not `v_s − u_s δ_old`.
   157	
   158	When the actual descended tower has `s' ≠ 2`, Φ-as-`s'=2` is a
   159	*truncation* to `(M_2', V_2')`. The compiler records it, and does **not**
   160	feed it to the `s = 2` shape (that would make `u' = d_2' − V_2'`
   161	negative on typical `s' ≥ 3` rows). Generalized Def 5.1(3) on the real
   162	`s'` tower is attempted separately; it hits a vanishing denominator on
   163	a majority of the excess (§5.2).
   164	
   165	### 2.3 (8)–(13) on the descended tower; what `s' = 2` means
   166	
   167	p.201 `SOURCE-READ`: (8) defines `A_{r-1}` from `δ_{r-1}` and
   168	`lcm(den δ_s, …, den δ_r)`; (9)(10)(11) constrain `V_{r-1}` for
   169	`r = s, …, 3`; (12)/(13) is the separate bottom (`r = 2`) condition.
   170	
   171	At `s' = 2`:
   172	
   173	- (8) is used to form `A_1'` from the Φ radii:
   174	  `L = den(δ_2')`, `A_1' = den(L · δ_1')`.
   175	- (10)/(11) are **vacuous** (`j` runs through the empty range
   176	  `s-1, …, 2`).
   177	- **Only (12)/(13) is active.**
   178	
   179	This is not an inference from a validator: it is the same loop as
   180	`Skel.full_ok` / `Skel.cond1011` in the charged skeleton.
   181	
   182	Φ-`(12)/(13)` on Moh's five, all pass:
   183	
   184	```text
   185	  (16,12) V2=3   A1=4  (12)  n*=4 m*=3
   186	  (21,14) V2=2   A1=3  (12)  n*=3 m*=2
   187	  (21,14) V2=5   A1=3  (12)
   188	  (15,10) V2=3   A1=2  (13)
   189	  (15,10) V2=2   A1=3  (12)
   190	```
   191	
   192	The p.188 identity `A_1 | (n*+m*)V_2 − 1` holds on these five.
   193	
   194	At `s' ≥ 3`, (10)/(11) at `j = s'-1, …, 2` *would* be active, but only
   195	after radii of the full descended `V`-path are defined. That is blocked
   196	on `OPEN[DEF51-MONOMIAL-MS-NMINUS2]` for 38 of the 52 excess rows.
   197	
   198	### 2.4 SHAPE: the general rule
   199	
   200	Parameters of an `s' = 2` descended pair: `K' = gcd(n', m') = deg_y h`,
   201	`d' = m'/K'`, `e' = n'/K'`, `d_2' = K'` on every row in this run,
   202	`u' = d_2' − V_2'`, `v' = V_2'`, `δ_1', δ_2'` from Φ,
   203	`deg_x h = u'`, `deg_x f = u' d'`, `deg_x g = u' e'`.
   204	
   205	**D1 order** (p.208 `ord h(σ) ≥ −δ_1` at `σ = π t^{δ_1}`, `x = t^{-1}`):
   206	
   207	```text
   208	  val(x^i y^j) = −i + δ_1 j
   209	  h:    i ≤ δ_1 (j+1),   i+j ≤ K,   i ≤ u',   j ≤ K
   210	  β:    i ≤ δ_1 (j+d'),  i+j ≤ m',  i ≤ deg_x f,  j ≤ K−1
   211	```
   212	
   213	**Leading-form fix, only when `δ_2' = −1`** (two points at infinity;
   214	Lemma 5.3 for constant `J`, and the monomial analogue
   215	`δ_s = −(k+1)/(n−M_s−1) = −1` when `n−M_s−1 = k+1`):
   216	
   217	```text
   218	  u' = 1:  y^{V_2}(y − x)                         # (16,12)
   219	  u' = 2:  y^{V_2}(y^2 − x^2)                     # (15,10) V2=3; p.210 three subdiscs
   220	  u' ≥ 3:  y^{V_2}(y − x)^{u'}                    # (15,10) V2=2: y^2(y−x)^3
   221	```
   222	
   223	The `u' = 2` split into two complementary linear factors is Moh p.210
   224	`SOURCE-READ`: *“the inverse transformation implies that there is a
   225	minor disc. Thus in the major disc `D_2` there are precisely three
   226	subdiscs which contains 2, 2, 6 of roots `f`.”* The compiler applies
   227	that split to every Prop 6.3 descendant with `u' = 2` and `δ_2' = −1`.
   228	Degree-`K` monomials not in the leading support are set to 0 (this is
   229	what kills `x y^4` in (15,10) `V_2 = 3`, which D1 alone would allow).
   230	Remaining free `h`-monomials are the D1-lower terms (`tot < K`).
   231	
   232	**A,B form of `β`, only when `δ_2' = −1` and `d' = 2`.** Horner:
   233	`h = y A + const`. Then `β = p A + q y + r x + s` (Moh (6); four
   234	parameters). This is the forced form Moh computes with, not a slice.
   235	When `δ_2' > −1` (one point at infinity) the `(y−x)` Horner is the
   236	*wrong* shape (descent-radii G2 warning); the compiler emits the full
   237	D1 monomial count and does not A,B-reduce.
   238	
   239	**Unknown counts emitted:**
   240	
   241	- `n_ord = #h_free + #β_D1 + 1` (`c`).  G2: 14+27+1 = **42**.
   242	- `n_ab  = #h_free + 4 + 1` when two-point `d' = 2`.  (15,10) `V_2=3`:
   243	  8+4+1 = 13; Moh computes with 12 (`c` not counted, or absorbed).
   244	
   245	`g = h^{e'} + G_{e'−2} h^{e'−2} + …` with `G_{e'−1} = 0`. For `d' = 2`,
   246	`e' = 3` the approximate-root expansion sets `G_1 = 3β`,
   247	`G_0 = (3/2)α` (`β^2 = α h + γ`). Those `G_i` are not extra unknowns
   248	at stage 2. Stage 1 (before the `η`-reduction) is Moh's 22 [15 or 13]
   249	and 17.
   250	
