+## 7. Typed general edge-map recipe
+
+**PROCEDURE (PROVED-HERE ALGEBRA; source availability may return OPEN).**
+
+```text
+type ParentNode = {
+  field, delta_parent, delta_child, prefix, centre C,
+  RawName -> (leading_weight lambda, centre_multiplicity w, raw_outer_unit),
+  child_kind: NonBottom | Bottom, normalization
+}
+type JetBand = {
+  ramification L, intermediate_shift B(u),
+  (RawName, integer_weight r) -> K_r(X),
+  identities certifying all K_r come from the same global f,g and named
+  approximate roots
+}
+type EdgeResult = {
+  child_initial[RawName], lower_coefficients, raw_leaders,
+  chart_action_matrix, defining_relations, provenance
+}
+
+EdgeMap(parent: ParentNode, band: JetBand)
+  -> EdgeResult | OPEN[missing band/map] | COUNTING-BOUND[counts]
+```
+
+1. Take (L) as a common denominator and set (u=t^{1/L});
+   (E=L(\delta_{child}-\delta_{parent})\) must be integral.
+2. Form the child chart
+   (X=C+B(u)+Yu^E), keeping inherited prefix coefficients as named ring
+   generators rather than existentially forgetting them.
+3. For each actual raw polynomial or approximate root (K), compute only
+   ([u^{wE}]\sum K_r^{(k)}(C)(B+Yu^E)^ku^r/k!). Its (Y^0,ldots,Y^{w-1})
+   coefficients are the child lower coefficients, with expressions in the
+   common band as provenance.
+4. Compute (h_C) and apply the appropriate outer powers. Use (5.1) only at
+   a non-bottom node satisfying its hypotheses; use (5.2)'s constant-RHS
+   bottom normalization at a bottom.
+5. Push (u\mapsto\zeta u) through every chart map and record the resulting
+   linear representation. State covariant or contravariant convention.
+6. Compare initials and characters to node-local families before elimination;
+   then declare the coefficient field, generator order, localization, positive
+   and negative controls. Return counts without eliminating above a cap.
+
+The `RawName` requirement matters: (q_j) and (q_{j-1}) use different
+approximate roots. If the band for the latter is absent, this procedure returns
+typed `OPEN`; it never substitutes the former merely because both are called
+(q).
+
