+# JET-EDGE-1612: one source-faithful common-jet edge
+
+Date: 2026-09-03  
+Lane: `jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903`  
+Verdict: **SUCCESS[ONE-EDGE]**; the general `OPEN[SOURCE-JET-GLUING]` remains open.
+
+## 0. Result
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** On Moh's reduced ((16,12)) configuration, one common
+ramification (u=t^{1/4}) and the literal common ((\bar g,\bar f,h)) of
+printed p.208 give the exact (D_2\to D_1) transition
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}h&=-P^3,\\
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}\bar g&=P^{12}-c_1P^8+c_5P^4-c_{13},\\
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}\bar f&=-P^9+c_3P^5-c_9P.
+\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{0.1}
+\]
+
+This is formula (3.5), not a Taylor expansion of stripped parent (p,q).
+The five active nonleading entries are the common-jet variables
+((c_1,c_3,c_5,c_9,c_{13})). In particular
+
+\[
+ [P^8]\operatorname{in}_{M}\bar g=-c_1
+   =[X^8]G_5(X),                                                  \tag{0.2}
+\]
+
+so a lower child coefficient is determined by the retained parent/common jet.
+It is not determined by the parent leading polynomial alone.
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** For a primitive fourth root (zeta), the covariant
+uniformizer action (u\mapsto\zeta u) is
+
+\[
+ (P,P_*)^T\longmapsto
+ \begin{pmatrix}\zeta&0\\0&\zeta^3\end{pmatrix}(P,P_*)^T,       \tag{0.3}
+\]
+
+where (P) is the major-chart coordinate and (P_*) is the compatible
+minor-truncation coordinate. On
+((g_M,f_M,g_*,f_*)) the character matrix is
+(operatorname{diag}(1,\zeta,1,\zeta)). This supplies the action matrix
+missing from the charged sibling projection for this edge only.
+
+**EXACT-CAS.** Before elimination, (0.1) was mapped term-for-term to the
+charged report's ((64,48)) bottom prototype. The largest elimination used
+7 variables, 0.0042 s, and the process peak was 52,156 KiB under enforced
+caps of 30 variables, 600 s, and 2 GiB. The local saturated component is
+nonunit, both localization-negative controls are unit, and elimination
+recovers (+ho^2=6).
+
+**NOT CLAIMED.** This is neither a global ((\bar f,\bar g)) witness nor a
+new exit price, and the compatible minor chart is not promoted to a recursive
+minor-child ODE. Neither ((90,60)) nor (D=108) was run.
+
+## 1. Custody and literal source data
+
+**HASH-VERIFIED.** An `awk` stream generated from
+`xmodel/jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903.run.v2` was passed directly to
+`sha256sum -c`; all 12 frozen files in `/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs` returned
+`OK`. No digest was retyped. The two requested 200-dpi source renders are
+[printed p.208 / PDF 69](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/jetedge-20260903/moh1983-printed-p208-pdf69.png)
+and [printed p.209 / PDF 70](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/jetedge-20260903/moh1983-printed-p209-pdf70.png),
+with SHA-256 respectively
+`550934c22fe5e0412e5b7e478f805da40317ddb299eaacf03040fb9049b4f354`
+and `19bbfa56fd017c545219fadc51fcc1e515a7faedc3ec059913eccacf133928a9`.
+
+**SOURCE-READ.** Printed p.207/PDF 68 gives
+((n,m,M_2,V_2,\delta_2,\delta_1,J)=(16,12,13,3,-1,1/4,X)) and
+(t=x^{-1}). It prints the major chart
+(sigma=\pi t^{1/4}) and the minor chart
+(sigma^*=t^{-1}+a_0+a_1t+a_2t^2+\pi t^3). Printed p.208 replaces the
+latter, for the coherent calculation, by the compatible truncation
+
+\[
+ \bar\sigma=t^{-1}+a_0+a_1t+a_2t^2+\pi t^{11/4}.                \tag{1.1}
+\]
+
+It calls ({\sigma,\bar\sigma}) a coherent complete system for the same
+(ar g) and (ar f=\bar T_1), and prints
+
+\[
+ \bar g=h^4+\alpha_1h^3+\alpha_2h^2+\alpha_3h+\alpha_4,
+ \qquad \bar f=h^3+\beta_2h+\beta_3.                            \tag{1.2}
+\]
+
+Here (h) is literally called the fourth approximate root of (ar f), and
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+ h=y^3(y-x)+b_1y^3+b_2y^2+b_3y+b_4=yA+b_4=y^2B+b_3y+b_4,\\
+ \alpha_2=c_1A+c_2,\quad \beta_2=c_3A+c_4,\\
+ \alpha_3=c_5A+c_5B+c_7,\quad \beta_3=c_8A+c_9B+c_{10},\\
+ \alpha_4=c_{11}A+c_{12}B+c_{13}(y-x).                         \tag{1.3}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+**SOURCE-LITERAL / AUDIT DELTA.** The source repeats (c_5) in (alpha_3)
+and has no (c_6); that agrees with its immediate count of 17 coefficients.
+The frozen compiler instead models distinct (c_5,c_6) and absorbs
+(alpha_1) to explain 17
+([compiler lines 253–292](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/appendix2-compiler-grok46-20260903.md:253)).
+No emendation was made here. `OPEN[PRINTED-C5-EMENDATION]` remains for any
+full-system reuse. It does not change (0.1): only the coefficient of (B)
+in (alpha_3) reaches the first major band, and that literal coefficient is
+(c_5).
+
+**TYPE SEPARATION.** (sigma), (sigma^*), and (ar\sigma) are three
+series roles; coherence is not an identification of their flags or physical
+places. The prefix symbols (a_1,a_2) in (1.1) are renamed
+`a1_prefix,a2_prefix` in the driver. Moh's later (a_i) in the p.209
+(eta)-Laurent display are not identified with them, and (eta) is not
+identified with (t).
+
+## 2. Rings and chart maps
+
+**DECLARED MAP.** The source coefficient ring, in generator order, is
+
+\[
+ R_0=\mathbf Q[b_1,b_2,b_3,b_4,\alpha_1,c_1,c_2,c_3,c_4,c_5,
+ c_7,c_8,c_9,c_{10},c_{11},c_{12},c_{13}],\qquad S=R_0[x,y].     \tag{2.1}
+\]
+
+Set (u=t^{1/4}). Distinct coefficient coordinates (X,P,P_*) give maps
+
+\[
+\begin{array}{rlll}
+ \phi_2:S&\to R_0[X]((u)),&x\mapsto u^{-4},&y\mapsto Xu^{-4},\\
+ \phi_M:S&\to R_0[P]((u)),&x\mapsto u^{-4},&y\mapsto Pu,\\
+ \phi_*:S&\to R_0[a_0,a'_1,a'_2,P_*]((u)),&x\mapsto u^{-4},&
+ y\mapsto u^{-4}+a_0+a'_1u^4+a'_2u^8+P_*u^{11}.
+                                                                    \tag{2.2}
+\end{array}
+\]
+
+Every generator of (R_0) maps identically. Thus the denominator-cleared
+edge gap is (E=4(1/4-(-1))=5), and (X=Pu^5) on the selected major
+recentring. The driver prints (2.1)–(2.2), the generator order, and verifies
+images of (h,A,B,\bar g,\bar f); matching glyphs are never used as a map.
+
+## 3. First-band extraction: formula (3.5)
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** Parent substitution gives
+
+\[
+ \phi_2(h)=u^{-16}\{X^3(X-1)+b_1X^3u^4+b_2X^2u^8
+                         +b_3Xu^{12}+b_4u^{16}\}.                \tag{3.1}
+\]
+
+At the selected centre (C=0), (h_0=X^3(X-1)) has multiplicity (3)
+and cofactor (h_C=(h_0/X^3)(0)=-1). Consequently the parent leading
+forms of (ar g,ar f) are (h_0^4,h_0^3), with centre multiplicities
+12 and 9 and leading (t)-powers (-16,-12).
+
+For (B(t)=0), the denominator-cleared form of the charged report's (3.5)
+is
+
+\[
+ I_K(P)=[u^{wE}]\sum_{r,k\ge0}{K_r^{(k)}(0)\over k!}
+                         P^ku^{r+kE}.                             \tag{3.2}
+\]
+
+The exact nonzero samples are:
+
+| raw (K) | (w) | target (u)-weight | ((\rho_t,k,\text{sample})) |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| (h) | 3 | 15 | ((0,3,-1)) |
+| (ar g) | 12 | 60 | ((0,12,1),(5,8,-c_1),(10,4,c_5),(15,0,-c_{13})) |
+| (ar f) | 9 | 45 | ((0,9,-1),(5,5,c_3),(10,1,-c_9)) |
+
+Here (+ho_t=r/4). Substitution into (3.2) yields (0.1), and direct
+coefficient extraction from (phi_M) gives the same three polynomials.
+Thus the first band has seven scalar slots, two fixed leaders and five active
+common-jet variables. The source ambient has 17 coefficient variables, but
+the requested transition needs only these five; no cap truncation was used.
+
+**SHARED-JET WITNESS.** Equation (0.2) is the earliest lower sample:
+(-c_1) comes from the (+ho_t=5) jet of the same global (ar g).
+Likewise (c_3,c_5,-c_9,-c_{13}) are shared samples. They would become free
+only after projecting away the common jet, exactly as diagnosed in the
+[charged Jet lemma](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/sibling-coefficients-sol56-20260903.md:216).
+
+## 4. Compatible minor and uniformizer action
+
+**PROVED-HERE / NOT A MINOR-CHILD ODE.** The principal part of
+(phi_*(h)) is
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ &(a_0+b_1)u^{-12}
+ +(3a_0^2+3a_0b_1+a'_1+b_2)u^{-8}\\
+ &+(3a_0^3+3a_0^2b_1+6a_0a'_1+2a_0b_2+3a'_1b_1+a'_2+b_3)u^{-4}
+ +P_*u^{-1}+O(1).
+\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{4.1}
+\]
+
+Moh's order bound cancels the first three coefficients, giving
+
+\[
+ a_0=-b_1,qquad a'_1=-b_2,qquad a'_2=-b_1b_2-b_3.              \tag{4.2}
+\]
+
+Then (operatorname{in}_*h=P_*), while the next coefficient is
+(H_0=b_1^2b_2+2b_1b_3+b_2^2+b_4). Exact valuations are
+(v_u(h,A,B,y-x)=(-1,3,4,0)); hence
+(operatorname{in}_*\bar g=P_*^4) and
+(operatorname{in}_*\bar f=P_*^3). This verifies that both restrictions
+really use the one common (h), without treating the minor series as another
+recursive child.
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** Work over
+(K_\zeta=\mathbf Q[\zeta]/(\zeta^2+1)). Under the covariant convention
+(u\mapsto\zeta u), with coefficient symbols fixed, the moving exponents
+are (1) and (11\equiv3\pmod4), proving (0.3). Both (h)-initials have
+character (zeta^3); both (f)-initials have character (zeta); both
+(g)-initials are invariant. The parent (X) is fixed because its exponent
+is (-4). The passive coordinate-ring convention that holds the physical
+series fixed uses the inverse matrix (operatorname{diag}(\zeta^3,\zeta)).
+
+## 5. Leading units and charged local family
+
+**PROVED-HERE, WITH HYPOTHESES.** If a parent factor is
+((X-C)^uH(X)), then recentering (X=C+Pu^E) makes the raw leading unit
+(H(C)); an outer power (r) makes it (H(C)^r). For the non-bottom
+exponents in the charged report this is exactly
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{lc}(p_{j-1})=h_C^{d_{j-1}/d_j},\qquad
+ \operatorname{lc}(q_{j-1})=h_C^{(n-M_{j-1})/d_j},              \tag{5.1}
+\]
+
+reproducing (3.7) when that non-bottom construction applies. This particular
+edge ends at the bottom, so its checked specialization is (3.8): with
+(h_C=-1),
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{lc}(g_M)=(-1)^{16/4}=1,qquad
+ \operatorname{lc}(f_M)=(-1)^{12/4}=-1.                         \tag{5.2}
+\]
+
+The sign is moved when (f_M) is made monic; no lower coefficient is inferred
+from (5.1) or (5.2).
+
+**MATCH-CHARGED, BEFORE ELIMINATION.** Put (z=P^4) and
+(-f_M=P F(z)). Then
+
+\[
+ G=z^3-c_1z^2+c_5z-c_{13},\qquad F=z^2-c_3z+c_9.                \tag{5.3}
+\]
+
+The charged local family (5.2) is obtained exactly by
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ c_1&=-s,&c_3&=-3s/4,&
+ c_5&=s^2(3/8-\rho/24),\\
+ c_9&=s^2(6-\rho)/32,&
+ c_{13}&=-s^3(4-\rho)/96,&\rho^2&=6.                            \tag{5.4}
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+
+The driver checks (5.3)–(5.4) identically before constructing any Gröbner
+basis and checks the action characters at the same stage. This is the
+node-local positive control of the
+[charged report, lines 515–560](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/sibling-coefficients-sol56-20260903.md:515),
+not a global Jacobian-pair witness.
+
+## 6. Bounded elimination
+
+**EXACT-CAS.** For monic (f_M), the bottom equation
+(D(4,3,g_M,f_M)=\kappa) gives, up to nonzero rational generator units,
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+3c_1-4c_3,quad c_1c_3-6c_5+8c_9,
+\quad5c_1c_9-9c_{13}-2c_3c_5,\\
+5c_{13}c_3-2c_5c_9,qquad \kappa+4c_{13}c_9.                    \tag{6.1}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+The declared lex ring is
+(mathbf Q[T,c_{13},c_9,c_5,c_3,\kappa,c_1]). The Rabinowitsch equation
+(T\kappa c_1-1) localizes at the bottom open condition (kappa\ne0) and
+at the charged-family scale chart (c_1\ne0); the latter is explicitly a
+chart choice, not a general bottom hypothesis. The ideal is nonunit (basis
+size 9). Adding (kappa=0), or adding (c_1=0), gives the unit ideal, so
+both localization-negative controls pass in the declared ring.
+
+The basis contains
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+-3c_1+4c_3,quad3c_1^2-24c_5+32c_9,
+\quad5c_1^3-24c_1c_5+96c_{13},\\
+25c_1^4-144c_1^2c_5+192c_5^2.                                  \tag{6.2}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+With (s=-c_1) and
+(+ho c_1^2=9c_1^2-24c_5), a second declared lex elimination in
+(mathbf Q[T_\rho,c_5,c_1,\rho]), localized by (T_\rho c_1-1), returns
+(+ho^2-6). Equations (6.2) then recover all of (5.4), and
+(kappa=-5s^5(\rho-3)/384\ne0). The triangular elimination for (4.2) uses
+6 variables and returns exactly its three displayed equations.
+
+Measured elimination times were 0.0031 s (minor tail), 0.0042 s (ODE),
+0.0014/0.0012 s (negative controls), and 0.0027 s (the (+ho) branch).
+All are exact rational computations. No `sat()` wrapper was used: the
+Rabinowitsch ideals themselves were extracted and tested.
+
+## 7. Typed general edge-map recipe
+
+**PROCEDURE (PROVED-HERE ALGEBRA; source availability may return OPEN).**
+
+```text
+type ParentNode = {
+  field, delta_parent, delta_child, prefix, centre C,
+  RawName -> (leading_weight lambda, centre_multiplicity w, raw_outer_unit),
+  child_kind: NonBottom | Bottom, normalization
+}
+type JetBand = {
+  ramification L, intermediate_shift B(u),
+  (RawName, integer_weight r) -> K_r(X),
+  identities certifying all K_r come from the same global f,g and named
+  approximate roots
+}
+type EdgeResult = {
+  child_initial[RawName], lower_coefficients, raw_leaders,
+  chart_action_matrix, defining_relations, provenance
+}
+
+EdgeMap(parent: ParentNode, band: JetBand)
+  -> EdgeResult | OPEN[missing band/map] | COUNTING-BOUND[counts]
+```
+
+1. Take (L) as a common denominator and set (u=t^{1/L});
+   (E=L(\delta_{child}-\delta_{parent})\) must be integral.
+2. Form the child chart
+   (X=C+B(u)+Yu^E), keeping inherited prefix coefficients as named ring
+   generators rather than existentially forgetting them.
+3. For each actual raw polynomial or approximate root (K), compute only
+   ([u^{wE}]\sum K_r^{(k)}(C)(B+Yu^E)^ku^r/k!). Its (Y^0,ldots,Y^{w-1})
+   coefficients are the child lower coefficients, with expressions in the
+   common band as provenance.
+4. Compute (h_C) and apply the appropriate outer powers. Use (5.1) only at
+   a non-bottom node satisfying its hypotheses; use (5.2)'s constant-RHS
+   bottom normalization at a bottom.
+5. Push (u\mapsto\zeta u) through every chart map and record the resulting
+   linear representation. State covariant or contravariant convention.
+6. Compare initials and characters to node-local families before elimination;
+   then declare the coefficient field, generator order, localization, positive
+   and negative controls. Return counts without eliminating above a cap.
+
+The `RawName` requirement matters: (q_j) and (q_{j-1}) use different
+approximate roots. If the band for the latter is absent, this procedure returns
+typed `OPEN`; it never substitutes the former merely because both are called
+(q).
+
+## 8. Appendix II comparison, FALLACY check, and readiness
+
+**YES, WITH A DECLARED COORDINATE.** The p.208 compatible-minor principal-tail
+cancellation (4.1)–(4.2) is exactly the (h)-component of this edge
+restriction. The p.209 (eta)-Laurent calculation likewise takes the
+polynomial part after expanding the same common (f,g,h): its relations
+(eta_2\beta_3=\gamma h+\gamma^*) and
+(eta_2^3=\delta h^2+\delta^*) cancel the negative tail of the formal
+(4/3)-power. It is an intra-coordinate instance of the same extraction
+operation, not by itself a two-chart map. Calling it a “(pi^{-1})-tail” is
+safe only after renaming the descended local coordinate (y) as
+(pi_{\rm loc}); Moh's p.207–208 (pi) is a free chart coefficient and
+p.209 uses (eta).
+
+**NO, NOT THE SHAPE RULE ALONE.** Compiler §2.4 and
+[`shape.py` lines 83–185](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/shape.py:83) correctly
+recover the valuation inequality, leading (y^3(y-x)), and four allowed
+lower (y)-monomials. They retain support, not the inherited prefix or common
+jet. Consequently they cannot output (4.2), (0.1), or (0.3). Appendix II's
+tail cancellation is the coefficient computation; SHAPE is its support
+precompiler.
+
+**FALLACY-v2 CHECK.** Chart series and physical places remain distinct; no
+minor ODE, pole identity, attainment, exit set, or charge is asserted. Raw
+leaders and monic normalization are separated. Rings, maps, orders, and
+localizations are explicit; zero and nonzero controls are reported. Prime
+marks here are labels except where a displayed (D) explicitly differentiates
+in (P). Therefore no `charge_basis` line is present.
+
+**READINESS, NOT EXECUTION.** The extraction kernel accepts a parent
+expression, leading weight, and multiplicity. Reuse requires supplying the new
+ramification, gap, intermediate (B), and the correct approximate-root bands;
+it is a checked template, not yet a whole-tree compiler. No frozen
+((90,60)) or (D=108) driver was imported or executed in this lane.
