+# JET-EDGE-1612: one source-faithful common-jet edge
+
+Date: 2026-09-03  
+Lane: jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903  
+Verdict: **SUCCESS[ONE-EDGE]**; general OPEN[SOURCE-JET-GLUING] remains open.
+
+## 0. Result
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** On Moh's reduced $(16,12)$ configuration, the common
+ramification $u=t^{1/4}$ and the literal common $(\bar g,\bar f,h)$ of
+printed p.208 give the exact $D_2\to D_1$ transition
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}h&=-P^3,\\
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}\bar g&=P^{12}-c_1P^8+c_5P^4-c_{13},\\
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}\bar f&=-P^9+c_3P^5-c_9P .
+\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{0.1}
+\]
+
+This is formula (3.5), not a Taylor expansion of stripped parent $p,q$.
+The active nonleading entries are the common-jet variables
+$(c_1,c_3,c_5,c_9,c_{13})$. In particular
+
+\[
+ [P^8]\operatorname{in}_{M}\bar g=-c_1=[X^8]G_5(X),              \tag{0.2}
+\]
+
+so one lower child coefficient is determined by the parent node plus the
+retained common band. It is not determined by the parent leading polynomial.
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** For a primitive fourth root $\zeta$, the covariant action
+$u\mapsto\zeta u$ on the two explicit chart coordinates is
+
+\[
+ (P,P_*)^T\longmapsto
+ \begin{pmatrix}\zeta&0\\0&\zeta^3\end{pmatrix}(P,P_*)^T.        \tag{0.3}
+\]
+
+On $(g_M,f_M,g_*,f_*)$ the character matrix is
+$\operatorname{diag}(1,\zeta,1,\zeta)$. This closes the charged action-map
+OPEN for this one edge only.
+
+**EXACT-CAS.** Before elimination, (0.1) was matched term-for-term to the
+charged local positive family. The largest elimination used 7 variables,
+0.0077 s, and process peak RSS was 52,424 KiB under enforced caps of 30
+variables, 600 s, and 2 GiB. The selected bottom-chart localization is
+nonunit and elimination recovers $\rho^2=6$.
+
+**NOT CLAIMED.** This is not a global $(\bar f,\bar g)$ witness, a new exit
+price, or a minor-child ODE. Neither $(90,60)$ nor $D=108$ was run.
+
+## 1. Custody and literal source
+
+**HASH-VERIFIED.** A manifest generated by awk directly from
+xmodel/jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903.run.v2 was piped to sha256sum -c; all 12
+frozen files in /tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs returned OK. No digest was
+retyped. The requested 200-dpi renders are
+[printed p.208 / PDF 69](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/jetedge-20260903/moh1983-printed-p208-pdf69.png)
+and [printed p.209 / PDF 70](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/jetedge-20260903/moh1983-printed-p209-pdf70.png).
+Their SHA-256 values are, respectively,
+550934c22fe5e0412e5b7e478f805da40317ddb299eaacf03040fb9049b4f354
+and 19bbfa56fd017c545219fadc51fcc1e515a7faedc3ec059913eccacf133928a9.
+
+**SOURCE-READ.** Printed p.207/PDF 68 gives
+$(n,m,M_2,V_2,\delta_2,\delta_1,J)=(16,12,13,3,-1,1/4,X)$ and $t=x^{-1}$.
+It prints the major chart $\sigma=\pi t^{1/4}$ and minor chart
+$\sigma^*=t^{-1}+a_0+a_1t+a_2t^2+\pi t^3$. Printed p.208 uses the compatible
+truncation
+
+\[
+ \bar\sigma=t^{-1}+a_0+a_1t+a_2t^2+\pi t^{11/4}.                \tag{1.1}
+\]
+
+It calls $\{\sigma,\bar\sigma\}$ a coherent complete system for the same
+$\bar g$ and $\bar f=\bar T_1$, and prints
+
+\[
+ \bar g=h^4+\alpha_1h^3+\alpha_2h^2+\alpha_3h+\alpha_4,\qquad
+ \bar f=h^3+\beta_2h+\beta_3.                                   \tag{1.2}
+\]
+
+Here $h$ is literally called the fourth approximate root of $\bar f$, and
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+ h=y^3(y-x)+b_1y^3+b_2y^2+b_3y+b_4=yA+b_4=y^2B+b_3y+b_4,\\
+ \alpha_2=c_1A+c_2,\quad \beta_2=c_3A+c_4,\\
+ \alpha_3=c_5A+c_5B+c_7,\quad \beta_3=c_8A+c_9B+c_{10},\\
+ \alpha_4=c_{11}A+c_{12}B+c_{13}(y-x).                          \tag{1.3}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+**SOURCE-LITERAL / AUDIT DELTA.** The page repeats $c_5$ in $\alpha_3$ and
+has no $c_6$; this agrees with its immediate count of 17 coefficients. No
+claim about Moh's intent and no emendation is made. The frozen compiler instead
+uses distinct $c_5,c_6$ and absorbs $\alpha_1$ to explain 17
+([compiler lines 253–292](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/appendix2-compiler-grok46-20260903.md:253)).
+OPEN[PRINTED-C5-EMENDATION] therefore remains for full-system reuse. It does
+not change this first band: only the printed coefficient of $B$ in
+$\alpha_3$ reaches (0.1).
+
+**TYPE SEPARATION.** The major series $\sigma$, actual minor series
+$\sigma^*$, and compatible truncation $\bar\sigma$ are distinct roles;
+coherence does not identify flags or physical places. Prefix symbols are
+renamed $a'_1,a'_2$ below. Moh's later $a_i$ in the p.209 $\eta$ display are
+not identified with them, and $\eta$ is not identified with $t$.
+
+## 2. Rings and maps
+
+**DECLARED MAP.** In the exact source order,
+
+\[
+ R_0=\mathbf Q[b_1,b_2,b_3,b_4,\alpha_1,c_1,c_2,c_3,c_4,c_5,
+ c_7,c_8,c_9,c_{10},c_{11},c_{12},c_{13}],\qquad S=R_0[x,y].     \tag{2.1}
+\]
+
+With $u=t^{1/4}$ and distinct coordinates $X,P,P_*$, the target Laurent rings
+and maps are
+
+\[
+\begin{array}{rlll}
+ R_2&=R_0[X][u,u^{-1}],&
+ \phi_2(x)=u^{-4},&\phi_2(y)=Xu^{-4},\\
+ R_M&=R_0[P][u,u^{-1}],&
+ \phi_M(x)=u^{-4},&\phi_M(y)=Pu,\\
+ R_*&=R_0[a_0,a'_1,a'_2,P_*][u,u^{-1}],&
+ \phi_*(x)=u^{-4},&
+ \phi_*(y)=u^{-4}+a_0+a'_1u^4+a'_2u^8+P_*u^{11}.
+                                                                    \tag{2.2}
+\end{array}
+\]
+
+The printed generator orders are $(R_0,X,u)$, $(R_0,P,u)$, and
+$(R_0,a_0,a'_1,a'_2,P_*,u)$; $u$ is then localized. Every $R_0$ generator
+maps identically. The driver constructs these dictionaries before
+substitution and mechanically checks every generator image. Thus the cleared
+edge gap is $E=4(1/4-(-1))=5$, with $X=Pu^5$ on the major recentring.
+
+## 3. Formula (3.5), first band
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** Parent substitution gives
+
+\[
+ \phi_2(h)=u^{-16}\{X^3(X-1)+b_1X^3u^4+b_2X^2u^8
+                         +b_3Xu^{12}+b_4u^{16}\}.                \tag{3.1}
+\]
+
+Define, in this descended chart,
+$p_2:=\operatorname{in}\phi_2(h)=X^3(X-1)$. The driver verifies
+$\operatorname{in}\phi_2(\bar g)=p_2^4$ and
+$\operatorname{in}\phi_2(\bar f)=p_2^3$. Thus $C=0$, its factor
+multiplicity in $p_2$ is $3$, $d_2=\gcd(16,12)=4$, and the cofactor of
+charged (3.6) is
+
+\[
+ h_C=\left.(p_2/X^3)\right|_{X=0}=-1.                            \tag{3.2}
+\]
+
+For the major chart the intermediate shift is $B(t)=0$. Formula (3.5), after
+clearing denominators, is
+
+\[
+ I_K(P)=[u^{wE}]\sum_{r,k\ge0}{K_r^{(k)}(0)\over k!}
+                         P^ku^{r+kE}.                            \tag{3.3}
+\]
+
+Its exact nonzero samples are:
+
+| raw $K$ | $w$ | target | $(\rho_t,k,\text{sample})$ |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| $h$ | 3 | $u^{15}$ | $(0,3,-1)$ |
+| $\bar g$ | 12 | $u^{60}$ | $(0,12,1),(5,8,-c_1),(10,4,c_5),(15,0,-c_{13})$ |
+| $\bar f$ | 9 | $u^{45}$ | $(0,9,-1),(5,5,c_3),(10,1,-c_9)$ |
+
+Here $\rho_t=r/4$. Formula (3.3) and direct extraction from $\phi_M$ both
+give (0.1). The band has seven scalar samples: two fixed leaders and five
+active common variables. The 17-variable source ambient is under cap, and
+no cap truncation occurred.
+
+**SHARED-JET WITNESS.** Equation (0.2) is the earliest lower sample:
+$-c_1=K^{(8)}_{\rho=5}(0)/8!$ comes from the same global $\bar g$.
+Likewise $c_3,c_5,-c_9,-c_{13}$ have recorded common-jet provenance. They
+become free only after projecting away this band, exactly as diagnosed by the
+[charged Jet lemma](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/sibling-coefficients-sol56-20260903.md:216).
+
+## 4. Compatible minor and action
+
+**PROVED-HERE / NOT A MINOR-CHILD ODE.** The principal part of $\phi_*(h)$ is
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ &(a_0+b_1)u^{-12}
+ +(3a_0^2+3a_0b_1+a'_1+b_2)u^{-8}\\
+ &+(3a_0^3+3a_0^2b_1+6a_0a'_1+2a_0b_2+3a'_1b_1+a'_2+b_3)u^{-4}
+ +P_*u^{-1}+O(1).
+\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{4.1}
+\]
+
+Moh's order bound cancels the first three coefficients:
+
+\[
+ a_0=-b_1,\qquad a'_1=-b_2,\qquad a'_2=-b_1b_2-b_3.             \tag{4.2}
+\]
+
+Then $\operatorname{in}_*h=P_*$ and the next coefficient is
+$H_0=b_1^2b_2+2b_1b_3+b_2^2+b_4$. Exact valuations
+$v_u(h,A,B,y-x)=(-1,3,4,0)$ force
+$\operatorname{in}_*\bar g=P_*^4$ and
+$\operatorname{in}_*\bar f=P_*^3$. This is a coherent second restriction,
+not a child pointer.
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** Work over
+$K_\zeta=\mathbf Q[\zeta]/(\zeta^2+1)$. Under the stated covariant convention,
+the moving exponents $1$ and $11\equiv3\bmod4$ prove (0.3). Both $h$ initials
+have character $\zeta^3$, both $f$ initials have character $\zeta$, and both
+$g$ initials are invariant. Parent $X$ is fixed because its exponent is
+$-4$. The passive convention holding the physical series fixed uses the
+inverse matrix $\operatorname{diag}(\zeta^3,\zeta)$.
+
+## 5. Leaders and the charged local family
+
+**GENERAL LEMMA, PROVED-HERE.** If a parent factor is
+$(X-C)^uH(X)$, recentering $X=C+Pu^E$ gives raw unit $H(C)$; an outer power
+$r$ gives $H(C)^r$. Applying this lemma to the non-bottom exponents derives
+the charged formula
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{lc}(p_{j-1})=h_C^{d_{j-1}/d_j},\qquad
+ \operatorname{lc}(q_{j-1})=h_C^{(n-M_{j-1})/d_j}.              \tag{5.1}
+\]
+
+**NOT-APPLICABLE HERE.** Equation (5.1), charged (3.7), is non-bottom and is
+not instantiated on this bottom edge. The actual endpoint verifies charged
+(3.8): using (3.2),
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{lc}(g_M)=(-1)^{16/4}=1,\qquad
+ \operatorname{lc}(f_M)=(-1)^{12/4}=-1.                         \tag{5.2}
+\]
+
+The sign moves when $f_M$ is made monic; neither leader identity determines
+lower monic coefficients.
+
+**MATCH-CHARGED, BEFORE ELIMINATION.** Put $z=P^4$ and
+$f_{\rm monic}=-f_M=P F(z)$. Then
+
+\[
+ G=z^3-c_1z^2+c_5z-c_{13},\qquad F=z^2-c_3z+c_9.                \tag{5.3}
+\]
+
+The charged family (5.2) is obtained exactly by
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ c_1&=-s,&c_3&=-3s/4,&c_5&=s^2(3/8-\rho/24),\\
+ c_9&=s^2(6-\rho)/32,&c_{13}&=-s^3(4-\rho)/96,&\rho^2&=6.
+                                                                    \tag{5.4}
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+
+The driver checks (5.3)–(5.4) and both action characters before any Gröbner
+basis. It also recomputes the nonzero discriminants and resultant printed in
+the [charged family](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/sibling-coefficients-sol56-20260903.md:515).
+This is that report's node-local positive control, not global existence.
+
+## 6. Bounded eliminations
+
+**EXACT-CAS / SELECTED LOCAL CHART.** The bottom equation
+$D(4,3,g_M,f_{\rm monic})=\kappa$ gives, up to rational units,
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+3c_1-4c_3,\quad c_1c_3-6c_5+8c_9,\quad
+5c_1c_9-9c_{13}-2c_3c_5,\\
+5c_{13}c_3-2c_5c_9,\qquad \kappa+4c_{13}c_9.                   \tag{6.1}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+The lex ring is
+$\mathbf Q[T,c_{13},c_9,c_5,c_3,\kappa,c_1]$. Adding
+$T\kappa c_1-1$ localizes at bottom openness $\kappa\ne0$ and the family
+chart $c_1\ne0$; the latter is a chart choice, not a general bottom
+hypothesis. The ideal is nonunit (basis size 9). Adding $\kappa=0$, or
+$c_1=0$, returns the unit ideal; these are explicitly localization-wiring
+controls, not collision exclusions. The substantive positive control is the
+exact family and invariant check above.
+
+The basis contains
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+-3c_1+4c_3,\quad3c_1^2-24c_5+32c_9,\quad
+5c_1^3-24c_1c_5+96c_{13},\\
+25c_1^4-144c_1^2c_5+192c_5^2.                                  \tag{6.2}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+With $s=-c_1$ and $\rho c_1^2=9c_1^2-24c_5$, lex elimination in
+$\mathbf Q[T_\rho,c_5,c_1,\rho]$, localized by $T_\rho c_1-1$, returns
+$\rho^2-6$ and recovers (5.4), including
+$\kappa=-5s^5(\rho-3)/384\ne0$. The 6-variable tail elimination returns
+exactly (4.2).
+
+One recorded final run took 2.40 s total; its eliminations were all below
+0.008 s. No sat() wrapper was used: the
+declared Rabinowitsch ideals themselves were tested.
+
+## 7. Typed general recipe
+
+**PROCEDURE (PROVED-HERE ALGEBRA; missing source data returns OPEN).**
+
+    type ParentNode = {
+      field, delta_parent, delta_child, prefix, centre C,
+      RawName -> (leading_weight, centre_multiplicity, raw_outer_unit),
+      child_kind: NonBottom | Bottom, normalization
+    }
+    type JetBand = {
+      ramification L, intermediate_shift B(u),
+      (RawName, integer_weight r) -> K_r(X),
+      common-global/approximate-root provenance
+    }
+    type EdgeResult = {
+      child_initial, lower_coefficients, raw_leaders,
+      chart_action_matrix, defining_relations, provenance
+    }
+    EdgeMap(ParentNode, JetBand)
+      -> EdgeResult | OPEN[missing band/map] | COUNTING-BOUND[counts]
+
+1. Set $u=t^{1/L}$ with all denominators cleared and
+   $E=L(\delta_{\rm child}-\delta_{\rm parent})\in\mathbf Z$.
+2. Form $X=C+B(u)+Yu^E$, retaining inherited-prefix coefficients as named
+   ring generators.
+3. For each actual raw polynomial or approximate root $K$, extract only
+   $[u^{wE}]\sum K_r^{(k)}(C)(B+Yu^E)^ku^r/k!$. Its coefficients below
+   $Y^w$ are the child lower coefficients, expressed in the common band.
+4. Apply the cofactor outer-power lemma. Use (5.1) only at a non-bottom node
+   satisfying its hypotheses; use the constant-RHS normalization at bottom.
+5. Push $u\mapsto\zeta u$ through each chart and state the action convention.
+6. Compare initials and characters before elimination; then declare field,
+   generator order, localization, controls, and cap counts.
+
+The RawName is essential: $q_j$ and $q_{j-1}$ use different approximate
+roots. If the latter band is absent, return typed OPEN rather than reuse the
+former.
+
+## 8. Appendix II comparison and readiness
+
+**YES, AFTER DECLARING THE COORDINATE.** The p.208 principal-tail cancellation
+(4.1)–(4.2) is precisely the $h$ component of a common edge restriction. The
+p.209 $\eta$ calculation similarly extracts the polynomial part for the same
+$f,g,h$ using
+$\beta_2\beta_3=\gamma h+\gamma^*$ and
+$\beta_2^3=\delta h^2+\delta^*$. It is an intra-coordinate instance of the
+same coefficient-extraction operation, not by itself a two-chart map.
+Calling it a “$\pi^{-1}$ tail” is safe only after renaming descended $y$ as
+$\pi_{\rm loc}$: Moh's p.207–208 $\pi$ is a chart coefficient and p.209 uses
+$\eta$.
+
+**NO, NOT SHAPE ALONE.** Compiler §2.4 and
+[shape.py lines 83–185](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/shape.py:83) recover the
+valuation inequality, leading $y^3(y-x)$, and four allowed lower
+$y$-monomials. They retain support, not inherited prefix or common jet, and
+therefore cannot output (4.2), (0.1), or (0.3). Tail cancellation is the
+coefficient computation; SHAPE is its support precompiler.
+
+**FALLACY-v2 CHECK.** Series roles and physical places remain distinct; no
+minor ODE, pole identity, attainment, exit, or charge is asserted. Raw and
+monic leaders are separated. Rings, maps, orders, localizations, and controls
+are explicit. Prime marks are labels except where $D$ explicitly differentiates
+in $P$. No charge_basis line is present.
+
+**READINESS, NOT EXECUTION.** The checked kernel accepts a parent expression,
+leading weight, and multiplicity. Reuse requires the new ramification, gap,
+intermediate $B$, and correct approximate-root bands; this is a template, not
+yet a whole-tree compiler. No $(90,60)$ or $D=108$ driver was imported or run.
