+## 5. Leaders and the charged local family
+
+**GENERAL LEMMA, PROVED-HERE.** If a parent factor is
+$(X-C)^uH(X)$, recentering $X=C+Pu^E$ gives raw unit $H(C)$; an outer power
+$r$ gives $H(C)^r$. Applying this lemma to the non-bottom exponents derives
+the charged formula
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{lc}(p_{j-1})=h_C^{d_{j-1}/d_j},\qquad
+ \operatorname{lc}(q_{j-1})=h_C^{(n-M_{j-1})/d_j}.              \tag{5.1}
+\]
+
+**NOT-APPLICABLE HERE.** Equation (5.1), charged (3.7), is non-bottom and is
+not instantiated on this bottom edge. The actual endpoint verifies charged
+(3.8): using (3.2),
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{lc}(g_M)=(-1)^{16/4}=1,\qquad
+ \operatorname{lc}(f_M)=(-1)^{12/4}=-1.                         \tag{5.2}
+\]
+
+The sign moves when $f_M$ is made monic; neither leader identity determines
+lower monic coefficients.
+
+**MATCH-CHARGED, BEFORE ELIMINATION.** Put $z=P^4$ and
+$f_{\rm monic}=-f_M=P F(z)$. Then
+
+\[
+ G=z^3-c_1z^2+c_5z-c_{13},\qquad F=z^2-c_3z+c_9.                \tag{5.3}
+\]
+
+The charged family (5.2) is obtained exactly by
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ c_1&=-s,&c_3&=-3s/4,&c_5&=s^2(3/8-\rho/24),\\
+ c_9&=s^2(6-\rho)/32,&c_{13}&=-s^3(4-\rho)/96,&\rho^2&=6.
+                                                                    \tag{5.4}
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+
+The driver checks (5.3)–(5.4) and both action characters before any Gröbner
+basis. It also recomputes the nonzero discriminants and resultant printed in
+the [charged family](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/sibling-coefficients-sol56-20260903.md:515).
+This is that report's node-local positive control, not global existence.
+
+## 6. Bounded eliminations
+
+**EXACT-CAS / SELECTED LOCAL CHART.** The bottom equation
+$D(4,3,g_M,f_{\rm monic})=\kappa$ gives, up to rational units,
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+3c_1-4c_3,\quad c_1c_3-6c_5+8c_9,\quad
+5c_1c_9-9c_{13}-2c_3c_5,\\
+5c_{13}c_3-2c_5c_9,\qquad \kappa+4c_{13}c_9.                   \tag{6.1}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+The lex ring is
+$\mathbf Q[T,c_{13},c_9,c_5,c_3,\kappa,c_1]$. Adding
+$T\kappa c_1-1$ localizes at bottom openness $\kappa\ne0$ and the family
+chart $c_1\ne0$; the latter is a chart choice, not a general bottom
+hypothesis. The ideal is nonunit (basis size 9). Adding $\kappa=0$, or
+$c_1=0$, returns the unit ideal; these are explicitly localization-wiring
+controls, not collision exclusions. The substantive positive control is the
+exact family and invariant check above.
+
+The basis contains
+
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+-3c_1+4c_3,\quad3c_1^2-24c_5+32c_9,\quad
+5c_1^3-24c_1c_5+96c_{13},\\
+25c_1^4-144c_1^2c_5+192c_5^2.                                  \tag{6.2}
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+
+With $s=-c_1$ and $\rho c_1^2=9c_1^2-24c_5$, lex elimination in
+$\mathbf Q[T_\rho,c_5,c_1,\rho]$, localized by $T_\rho c_1-1$, returns
+$\rho^2-6$ and recovers (5.4), including
+$\kappa=-5s^5(\rho-3)/384\ne0$. The 6-variable tail elimination returns
+exactly (4.2).
+
+One recorded final run took 2.40 s total; its eliminations were all below
+0.008 s. No sat() wrapper was used: the
+declared Rabinowitsch ideals themselves were tested.
+
+## 7. Typed general recipe
+
+**PROCEDURE (PROVED-HERE ALGEBRA; missing source data returns OPEN).**
+
+    type ParentNode = {
+      field, delta_parent, delta_child, prefix, centre C,
+      RawName -> (leading_weight, centre_multiplicity, raw_outer_unit),
+      child_kind: NonBottom | Bottom, normalization
+    }
+    type JetBand = {
+      ramification L, intermediate_shift B(u),
+      (RawName, integer_weight r) -> K_r(X),
+      common-global/approximate-root provenance
+    }
+    type EdgeResult = {
+      child_initial, lower_coefficients, raw_leaders,
+      chart_action_matrix, defining_relations, provenance
+    }
+    EdgeMap(ParentNode, JetBand)
+      -> EdgeResult | OPEN[missing band/map] | COUNTING-BOUND[counts]
+
+1. Set $u=t^{1/L}$ with all denominators cleared and
+   $E=L(\delta_{\rm child}-\delta_{\rm parent})\in\mathbf Z$.
+2. Form $X=C+B(u)+Yu^E$, retaining inherited-prefix coefficients as named
+   ring generators.
+3. For each actual raw polynomial or approximate root $K$, extract only
+   $[u^{wE}]\sum K_r^{(k)}(C)(B+Yu^E)^ku^r/k!$. Its coefficients below
+   $Y^w$ are the child lower coefficients, expressed in the common band.
+4. Apply the cofactor outer-power lemma. Use (5.1) only at a non-bottom node
+   satisfying its hypotheses; use the constant-RHS normalization at bottom.
+5. Push $u\mapsto\zeta u$ through each chart and state the action convention.
+6. Compare initials and characters before elimination; then declare field,
+   generator order, localization, controls, and cap counts.
+
+The RawName is essential: $q_j$ and $q_{j-1}$ use different approximate
+roots. If the latter band is absent, return typed OPEN rather than reuse the
+former.
+
+## 8. Appendix II comparison and readiness
+
+**YES, AFTER DECLARING THE COORDINATE.** The p.208 principal-tail cancellation
+(4.1)–(4.2) is precisely the $h$ component of a common edge restriction. The
+p.209 $\eta$ calculation similarly extracts the polynomial part for the same
+$f,g,h$ using
+$\beta_2\beta_3=\gamma h+\gamma^*$ and
+$\beta_2^3=\delta h^2+\delta^*$. It is an intra-coordinate instance of the
+same coefficient-extraction operation, not by itself a two-chart map.
+Calling it a “$\pi^{-1}$ tail” is safe only after renaming descended $y$ as
+$\pi_{\rm loc}$: Moh's p.207–208 $\pi$ is a chart coefficient and p.209 uses
+$\eta$.
+
+**NO, NOT SHAPE ALONE.** Compiler §2.4 and
+[shape.py lines 83–185](/tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs/shape.py:83) recover the
+valuation inequality, leading $y^3(y-x)$, and four allowed lower
+$y$-monomials. They retain support, not inherited prefix or common jet, and
+therefore cannot output (4.2), (0.1), or (0.3). Tail cancellation is the
+coefficient computation; SHAPE is its support precompiler.
+
+**FALLACY-v2 CHECK.** Series roles and physical places remain distinct; no
+minor ODE, pole identity, attainment, exit, or charge is asserted. Raw and
+monic leaders are separated. Rings, maps, orders, localizations, and controls
+are explicit. Prime marks are labels except where $D$ explicitly differentiates
+in $P$. No charge_basis line is present.
+
+**READINESS, NOT EXECUTION.** The checked kernel accepts a parent expression,
+leading weight, and multiplicity. Reuse requires the new ramification, gap,
+intermediate $B$, and correct approximate-root bands; this is a template, not
+yet a whole-tree compiler. No $(90,60)$ or $D=108$ driver was imported or run.
