+## 4. Compatible minor and action
+
+**PROVED-HERE / NOT A MINOR-CHILD ODE.** The principal part of $\phi_*(h)$ is
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ &(a_0+b_1)u^{-12}
+ +(3a_0^2+3a_0b_1+a'_1+b_2)u^{-8}\\
+ &+(3a_0^3+3a_0^2b_1+6a_0a'_1+2a_0b_2+3a'_1b_1+a'_2+b_3)u^{-4}
+ +P_*u^{-1}+O(1).
+\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{4.1}
+\]
+
+Moh's order bound cancels the first three coefficients:
+
+\[
+ a_0=-b_1,\qquad a'_1=-b_2,\qquad a'_2=-b_1b_2-b_3.             \tag{4.2}
+\]
+
+Then $\operatorname{in}_*h=P_*$ and the next coefficient is
+$H_0=b_1^2b_2+2b_1b_3+b_2^2+b_4$. Exact valuations
+$v_u(h,A,B,y-x)=(-1,3,4,0)$ force
+$\operatorname{in}_*\bar g=P_*^4$ and
+$\operatorname{in}_*\bar f=P_*^3$. This is a coherent second restriction,
+not a child pointer.
