+# JET-EDGE-1612: one source-faithful common-jet edge
+
+Date: 2026-09-03  
+Lane: jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903  
+Verdict: **SUCCESS[ONE-EDGE]**; general OPEN[SOURCE-JET-GLUING] remains open.
+
+## 0. Result
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** On Moh's reduced $(16,12)$ configuration, the common
+ramification $u=t^{1/4}$ and the literal common $(\bar g,\bar f,h)$ of
+printed p.208 give the exact $D_2\to D_1$ transition
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}h&=-P^3,\\
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}\bar g&=P^{12}-c_1P^8+c_5P^4-c_{13},\\
+ \operatorname{in}_{M}\bar f&=-P^9+c_3P^5-c_9P .
+\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{0.1}
+\]
+
+This is formula (3.5), not a Taylor expansion of stripped parent $p,q$.
+The active nonleading entries are the common-jet variables
+$(c_1,c_3,c_5,c_9,c_{13})$. In particular
+
+\[
+ [P^8]\operatorname{in}_{M}\bar g=-c_1=[X^8]G_5(X),              \tag{0.2}
+\]
+
+so one lower child coefficient is determined by the parent node plus the
+retained common band. It is not determined by the parent leading polynomial.
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** For a primitive fourth root $\zeta$, the covariant action
+$u\mapsto\zeta u$ on the two explicit chart coordinates is
+
+\[
+ (P,P_*)^T\longmapsto
+ \begin{pmatrix}\zeta&0\\0&\zeta^3\end{pmatrix}(P,P_*)^T.        \tag{0.3}
+\]
+
+On $(g_M,f_M,g_*,f_*)$ the character matrix is
+$\operatorname{diag}(1,\zeta,1,\zeta)$. This closes the charged action-map
+OPEN for this one edge only.
+
+**EXACT-CAS.** Before elimination, (0.1) was matched term-for-term to the
+charged local positive family. The largest elimination used 7 variables,
+0.0077 s, and process peak RSS was 52,424 KiB under enforced caps of 30
+variables, 600 s, and 2 GiB. The selected bottom-chart localization is
+nonunit and elimination recovers $\rho^2=6$.
+
+**NOT CLAIMED.** This is not a global $(\bar f,\bar g)$ witness, a new exit
+price, or a minor-child ODE. Neither $(90,60)$ nor $D=108$ was run.
+
+## 1. Custody and literal source
+
+**HASH-VERIFIED.** A manifest generated by awk directly from
+xmodel/jet-edge-1612-sol56-20260903.run.v2 was piped to sha256sum -c; all 12
+frozen files in /tmp/jc2-lane.HTDIrG/inputs returned OK. No digest was
+retyped. The requested 200-dpi renders are
+[printed p.208 / PDF 69](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/jetedge-20260903/moh1983-printed-p208-pdf69.png)
+and [printed p.209 / PDF 70](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/jetedge-20260903/moh1983-printed-p209-pdf70.png).
+Their SHA-256 values are, respectively,
+550934c22fe5e0412e5b7e478f805da40317ddb299eaacf03040fb9049b4f354
+and 19bbfa56fd017c545219fadc51fcc1e515a7faedc3ec059913eccacf133928a9.
+
+**SOURCE-READ.** Printed p.207/PDF 68 gives
+$(n,m,M_2,V_2,\delta_2,\delta_1,J)=(16,12,13,3,-1,1/4,X)$ and $t=x^{-1}$.
+It prints the major chart $\sigma=\pi t^{1/4}$ and minor chart
+$\sigma^*=t^{-1}+a_0+a_1t+a_2t^2+\pi t^3$. Printed p.208 uses the compatible
+truncation
+
+\[
+ \bar\sigma=t^{-1}+a_0+a_1t+a_2t^2+\pi t^{11/4}.                \tag{1.1}
+\]
+
+It calls $\{\sigma,\bar\sigma\}$ a coherent complete system for the same
+$\bar g$ and $\bar f=\bar T_1$, and prints
